    "body": "### Problem\n\nWith ui2 enabled and 'cmdheight' 0, when a message is displayed before running a command with an interactive prompt (such as `:%s///c`), `cmdline_hide()` schedules closing the expanded cmd window. That scheduled callback runs after `cmdline_show()` has already opened the confirmation prompt, and `check_targets()` reopens the cmd window hidden because 'cmdheight' is 0, making the prompt invisible.\n\n### Solution\n\n1. In `cmdline_hide()`, guard closing the cmd window if another prompt or cmdline has already become active (`not M.prompt and M.level == 0`).\n2. Ensure the dialog window holding pending messages is cleared if the completed cmdline was not a prompt (`not was_prompt or M.level == 0`).\n\nFixes #42116\n\nAI-assisted",
